{"ideviceId":"idevice-1785610672133-mo8u9186b","textInfoDurationInput":"","textInfoDurationTextInput":"Duration","textInfoParticipantsInput":"","textInfoParticipantsTextInput":"Grouping","textTextarea":"<p>HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language. It organizes the content of a webpage using elements called tags. For example, HTML tags can create headings, paragraphs, images, links, and buttons.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;br&gt;&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;title&gt;My First Webpage&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;h1&gt;Welcome to My Webpage&lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;This is my first paragraph.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;button&gt;Click Me&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
<pre><br /></pre>
<pre><code>The &lt;h1&gt; element creates the main heading, the &lt;p&gt; element creates a paragraph, and the &lt;button&gt; element creates a button. At this point, the button will appear on the page, but it will not perform an action until JavaScript is added later.</code></pre>
<pre><br /><br /></pre>
<p><br /><br /></p>","textFeedbackInput":"Show Feedback","textFeedbackTextarea":""}
